read AGENTS.md in the repo root before anything else. it is the master context for any agent working here (claude, cursor, codex).

then read PLAN.md for architecture and PROGRESS.md for current state and what to do next.

key conventions to apply on every response:

writing style:
- lowercase throughout. caps only for acronyms and proper nouns.
- no em dashes. use periods, commas, colons, parens.
- short sentences, direct, opinionated. no hedging when the answer is clear.
- minimal formatting. headers for sections, bold only when introducing a key term.

code style:
- simple over abstract. an undergrad should read it in one pass.
- no helpers for things done once.
- short variable names.
- no defensive handling for things that won't fail on clean inputs.
- only validate at system boundaries (user input, external APIs).

design (quiet utility):
- neutral surfaces, soft shadows, indigo-300 as the only accent.
- phosphor icons at 20px regular weight.
- font: Ronzino or geometric/humanist sans, -0.02em letter-spacing.
- if an element doesn't carry information, it shouldn't exist.

workflow:
- work in phases as defined in PLAN.md. one phase at a time.
- before ending the session, append 2-3 lines to PROGRESS.md (state, next step, blockers).
- commit work in progress, even as WIP commits. git is the cross-agent audit trail.
